# GDR cards: rooms, scenes and game flow for the Godot rebuild (planner: Sonnet 5.5, 14 Oct 2026).
# Contracts: docs/GODOT_PLANNER_BRIEF.md, aligned with the GDF / GDS / GDU specs (UiButton GDU02, UiMenu GDU03, Main + stage GDU08,
# Tv GDU10/GDU12, SceneHost GDU30, TestFakeGame GDU28, Game + CoreSave GDF09/GDF10, SimEndGame GDS08 ...).
# Invented HERE (other planners must match): RoomHotspot (invisible tap rect), RoomBase (layers Background/Props/Characters/Lights/Front + Ui + Hotspots),
# TapUtil (test helper), Flow (child of Main, navigation + lifecycle), Transitions node, room hooks enter(params) / exit() (SceneHost hooks).
MODE = "godot"

JS = "/Users/leelangley/wt/webbwheresmycar/_dev/"
GODOT = "docs/GODOT.md (plan, TV-centred layout, tap rule, determinism) and docs/GODOT_PLANNER_BRIEF.md section SHARED CONTRACTS (Game, Data, Sim*, Core*, tests, tools)"
ZONES = "STAGE ZONES (1280x720): banner y 0..120, tableau y 120..590, HUD strip y 590..720. The Main scene (GDU08) draws the Hud and Banner above the room; a room keeps every tappable rect inside y 120..590 (the TV and the characters may overlap the zones a little)."
TESTS = "Tests: `godot/tests/test_<name>.gd` starts with `extends \"res://tests/harness.gd\"`; every method named `test_*` runs; helpers `ok(cond, msg)`, `eq(a, b, msg)`, `near(a, b, eps, msg)`. Run one file with `sh tools/godot/gtest.sh test_<name>` (last line `GDTEST OK`)."
HYGIENE = "Test hygiene: get the tree with `var tree := Engine.get_main_loop() as SceneTree`; add a node with `tree.root.add_child(n)` when its `_ready` must run; at the end of each test `tree.root.remove_child(n)` (if added) and `n.free()`. Nodes made with `.new()` and never added can simply be `free()`d."
UIAPI = "Widgets from the GDU cards that rooms use: `UiButton` (godot/ui/button.gd: `UiButton.new()`, vars `text` (up to 2 lines, split on \\n), `kind` 'normal'|'primary'|'remote'|'card', `enabled`, `hot` (gold outline = selected), signals `activated` and `blocked` (a tap on a DISABLED button), `handle_event(ev)`, minimum size 64x64); `UiTap` (godot/ui/tap.gd: `press(id)`, `release(id) -> bool`); `UiMenu` (godot/ui/menu.gd: `open(list: Array[String], at: Vector2)`, `set_item_enabled(i, on)`, signal `chosen(index: int)`, closes itself when a row is chosen, rows 64 px, width 280); `UiTheme` (godot/ui/ui_theme.gd: `title_font()`, `body_font()`, `color(key)`)."
FAKE = "Test double for the Game autoload: `TestFakeGame.new()` (godot/tests/fake_game.gd, GDU28). Its `state` is the sample state: day 12, cash 12345, reputation 40, garageSlots 3, cars `c1` (modelId t1_allergy, owned, condition 6.0, fault null) and `c2` (t1_robbin, owned, condition 9.0, fault `{faultId: 'puncture', label: 'Flat tyre', cost: 80, severity: 'minor'}`, rentMonthly 0, rentedAtCondition null), 3 shop listings, 2 requests, stats.jobsDone 2, plates all false, auction `{month 1, lots [], consigned [], lastResults []}`, flags `{gameOver false, won false, reason ''}`. `act(action, params)` appends `{action, params}` to `acts`, returns a copy of `next_result` (default `{ok: true, msg: 'Done'}`), emits `changed` when ok is true and `toast_requested(msg)` when ok is false with a message; `toasts` collects the toast texts; signals `changed`, `toast_requested`, `day_advanced`, `game_over`. A room gets it with `room.game = TestFakeGame.new()` BEFORE it is added to the tree."
TAP = "Tapping in tests: `TapUtil.tap(control)` (godot/tests/tap_util.gd, GDR32) does press then release inside on ANY control that has `handle_event(ev)` (UiButton, RoomHotspot, UiMenu); `TapUtil.press(c)`, `TapUtil.release(c)`, `TapUtil.tap_away(c)` (press inside, release outside: must NOT activate); positions default to `Vector2(5, 5)` (inside) and `TapUtil.OUTSIDE`; for a UiMenu row pass a position such as `Vector2(20, 8 + 64 * i + 10)`."
ROOMAPI = "godot/rooms/room_base.gd (GDR19, class `RoomBase extends Control`): `LAYER_NAMES`, `build_layers()`, `layer(name)`, `placeholder(name)`, `ui()`, `set_plate(layer, tex, pos)`, `add_hotspot(id, rect) -> RoomHotspot` (invisible tap rect), `add_button(id, rect, text, kind) -> UiButton`, `hotspots` (id -> control, both kinds), `game` + `get_game()`, signals `request_scene(scene_id: StringName, params: Dictionary)`, `chatter(text)`, `toast(text)`, virtuals `enter(params)`, `exit()`, `_on_hotspot(id)`, `_on_button_blocked(id)`, `_on_button_down(id)`, statics `add_box`, `add_panel`, `add_label`, `pixel_font`. Rooms are built IN CODE in `_ready` (the .tscn is only a root Control with the script), so every node name in a card is an exact contract for the art cards (GDA) and the tests. Rooms are shown by the SceneHost (GDU30), which calls `enter(params)` after adding and `exit()` before removing."
ACT = "Game.act actions this card uses (GDS20 dispatch; results are Dictionaries `{ok: bool, msg: String}`; parameter keys are camelCase like the state): `wait_day` (the kettle: one day passes), `service_car {carId, kind: 'quick'|'full'}`, `fix_fault {carId}`, `restore_car {carId}`, `sell_to_dealer {carId}`, `return_rental {carId}`, `consign_car {carId, reserve}`, `unconsign {carId}`, `attend_auction {}`, `reveal_stat {lotId, stat}`, `place_bid {lotId, steps}`. The Game itself emits `toast_requested(msg)` for every REFUSED action, saves after every successful one, and emits `day_advanced` / `changed` / `game_over`: rooms therefore never toast a refusal themselves (they would show twice); they only toast the success messages the JS scenes toasted."
SHOT = "Screenshot step: run `sh tools/godot/gshot.sh {scene} /tmp/{name}.png 8`, then LOOK at the PNG with the Read tool and describe it in your final reply (what is where, anything overlapping, anything off screen). If the screenshot step fails because a card it needs is not merged, say so, do not fake it."

